{"authored" [{"question" "q-129634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x,y)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(1,-1)=-2,\\,{f}_{x}(1,-1)=1,\\,{f}_{y}(1,-1)=6.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-1),$ estimate the value of $f(0.96,-0.95).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(1,-1)+∇f(1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =f(1,-1)+⟨{f}_{x}(1,-1),{f}_{y}(1,-1)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1⟩ \\\\  & =-2+⟨1,6⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(0.96,-0.95)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=0.96$ and $y=-0.95,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.96,-0.95) & ≈-2+⟨1,6⟩\\cdot ⟨0.96-1,-0.95+1⟩ \\\\  & =-2+⟨1,6⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.04,0.05⟩ \\\\  & =-2+1(-0.04)+6(0.05) \\\\  & =-2-0.04+0.3 \\\\  & =-1.74\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ec23d17fb67e890f41a65ae1ac28efe96d7fe546dc24470d93799900dc2cff6" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1.74"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1.85"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1.97"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2.04"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2.11"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $f(x,y,z)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,2,-3)=-6, & \\,{f}_{x}(x,y,z)=yz,\\,{f}_{y}(x,y,z)=xz,\\,{f}_{z}(x,y,z)=xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,2,-3),$ estimate the value of $f(1.01,1.95,-3.02).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,2,-3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,2,-3)+∇f(1,2,-3)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z+3⟩ \\\\  & =-6+⟨{f}_{x}(1,2,-3),{f}_{y}(1,2,-3),{f}_{z}(1,2,-3)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z+3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{x}(1,2,-3)$, ${f}_{y}(1,2,-3)$ and ${f}_{z}(1,2,-3),$ using the given partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,2,-3) & =2(-3)=-6 \\\\ {f}_{y}(1,2,-3) & =1(-3)=-3 \\\\ {f}_{z}(1,2,-3) & =1(2)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈-6+⟨-6,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z+3⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(1.01,1.95,-3.02)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=1.01,y=1.95$ and $z=-3.02,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.01,1.95,-3.02) & ≈-6+⟨-6,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨1.01-1,1.95-2,-3.02+3⟩ \\\\  & =-6+⟨-6,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨0.01,-0.05,-0.02⟩ \\\\  & =-6-0.06+0.15-0.04 \\\\  & =-5.95\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ec23d17fb67e890f41a65ae1ac28efe96d7fe546dc24470d93799900dc2cff6" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5.87"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5.95"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5.98"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6.01"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6.12"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129657" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x,y,z)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(1,2,3)=6,\\,{f}_{x}(1,2,3)=6,\\,{f}_{y}(1,2,3)=3,\\,{f}_{z}(1,2,3)=2.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,2,3)$ estimate the value of $f(1.08,1.93,3.05)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129657" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,2,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,2,3)+∇f(1,2,3)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z-3⟩ \\\\  & =6+⟨{f}_{x}(1,2,3),{f}_{y}(1,2,3),{f}_{z}(1,2,3)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z-3⟩ \\\\  & =6+⟨6,3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(1.08,1.93,3.05)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=1.08,$ $y=1.93,$ and $z=3.05$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.08,1.93,3.05) & ≈6+⟨6,3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨1.08-1,1.93-2,3.05-3⟩ \\\\  & =6+⟨6,3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨0.08,-0.07,0.05⟩ \\\\  & =6+6(0.08)+3(-0.07)+2(0.05) \\\\  & =6+0.48-0.21+0.1 \\\\  & =6.37\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129657" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ec23d17fb67e890f41a65ae1ac28efe96d7fe546dc24470d93799900dc2cff6" "basis" 1859 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129657" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057928/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd56eab8b5bc9f63d984b6c9ea8be9d43a273cac3967932c65823073636be38c" "basis" 1859 "verificati